{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Gahvaratīriya","html":"<article id='thag1.31'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.31 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.31 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Catutthavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Four </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Gahvaratīriyattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Gahvaratīriya </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Phuṭṭho ḍaṁsehi makasehi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Pestered by flies and mosquitoes </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>araññasmiṁ brahāvane; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>in the wilds, the formidable forest, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Nāgo saṅgāmasīseva, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>one should mindfully endure, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sato tatrādhivāsaye”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>like an elephant at the head of the battle. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Gahvaratīriyo thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
